Polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS),you are born with pcos but symptoms often start during puberty although for some people this can beryllium later up to their early twenties there are lots of different symptoms that can be caused by pcos the main symptoms are other symptom can include people who have pcos can also struggle with depression and with theirmental healthas a result of the condition pcos can increase your risk of certain health conditions including type 2 diabetes and high cholesterol you should speak to your doctor if you are experiencing these symptoms and you are not pregnant or on hormone treatment you can use ourmenstrual health symptom questionnaire pdf 421kb to keep a note of your symptomsand how you re feeling you can print it and talk about it with your healthcare professional to help them understand the different symptoms you re experiencing,,,
Thyroid cancer,in its early stages thyroid cancer tends to cause no or very few symptoms the main symptom of thyroid cancer is a lump or swelling at the front of the neck just below your adam s apple which is usually painless women besides have adam s apples but they re much smaller and less prominent than a man s the lymph nodes in your neck can also be affected and become swollen lymph nodes are small glands that are part of the lymphatic system which helps fight infection other symptom of thyroid cancer only tend to occur after the condition has reached an advanced stage and may include,,,
Lipoedema,people with lipoedema usually have a small waist but large hips and thighs their upper body and lower berth body can be completely different sizes this makes it difficult to shop for clothes that fit right symptoms can include lipoedema can be linked tomental healthproblems for exampledepression anxiety and disordered eating speak to your doctor if you are experiencing any of these symptoms they ll be able to give you help and advice on how to pull off your symptoms other health conditions likelymphoedema can cause large or swollen legs sometimes people with lipoedema can also develop this condition,,,
Postnatal depression,postnatal depression affect everyone differently it can start at any point in the first year after giving birth it may develop suddenly or gradually it can also continue from depression during pregnancy many people feel a bit down tearful or anxious in the first week after giving birth this is often called the baby blues and doesn t last for more than 2 weeks after giving birth if your symptoms stopping point longer or start later you could have postnatal depression the main symptoms of postnatal depression include these symptoms can affect your day to day life and your relationships with your baby family and friends,,,
