Sciatica,sciatica can have a range of symptoms these can include a change in feeling in the leg or foot can include,"Sciatica can be caused by irritation of the nerves which travel from the spine down the legs.  This can be from inflammation around the nerves and in some cases from pressure, usually from a disc related change. Most symptoms of sciatica will improve with time. Nerves are resilient and in most cases inflammation and any disc changes resolve allowing nerves to recover.",,"Most people will recover from sciatica with a combination of time, modifying activity, and pacing themselves to allow the nerves to adapt. Pain medication, staying active, and gentle exercise will also help. The nerve can still be sensitive so it is recommended to build up your tolerance to activities slowly.  The little and often approach to movement is recommended. There are some things you can do to help manage this condition yourself."
