Diabetic retinopathy,you won t usually notice diabetic retinopathy in the early stages as it doesn t tend to have any obvious symptom until it s more advanced however early signs of the condition can beryllium picked up by taking photographs of the eyes duringdiabetic eye screening contact your optician immediately if you experience these symptoms don t necessarily mean you have diabetic retinopathy but it s important to get them checked out don t wait until your next screening appointment,,,
Ovarian cancer,the symptoms of ovarian cancer can be difficult to recognise particularly in information technology early stages this is because they are often the same as symptoms of other less serious conditions such asirritable bowel syndrome ibs or pre menstrual syndrome pms however 3 main symptoms are more frequent other symptoms such as back pain needing to pass urine more frequently than usual and pain during sex may be the result of other conditions in the pelvic area however they may be a sign of ovarian cancer if you have these types of symptoms try keeping a diary to record how many of these symptoms you have over a longer period bear in mind that ovarian cancer is rare in women and anyone with ovaries under 40 years of age speak to your gp if you rich person these symptoms regularly on most days for 3 weeks or more although it s unlikely they re being caused by a serious problem it s best to check if you ve already seen your gp and the symptoms continue or get worse you should go back and explain this you know your body better than anyone,,,
Chronic fatigue syndrome,the symptoms of me cfs can be different for everyone there may be times when your symptoms improve and you ll be able to do some everyday activities at other times symptoms may get worse affecting your daily life not everyone will experience all of the symptoms if you experience new symptoms talk to your gp or specialist as the new symptoms may be unrelated to me cfs if you have periods you may find your symptoms get worse at different times during your menstrual cycle there are 4 main symptoms of me cfs me cfs can cause debilitating fatigue that is post exertional malaise pem is where symptoms get worse even after little physical or mental activity if you have pem you might find symptoms get worse hours or days after the activity you might find your symptoms are not in proportion to the amount of activity that has been done it can take a hanker time to recover from pem the symptoms might last hours days weeks or longer you might wake up feeling unrefreshed after sleep you might also experience sleep disturbance you might me cfs can cause cognitive difficulties sometimes described as brain fog this can include simple physical or mental activities or combinations of activities can leave people with me cfs feeling wholly exhausted it can also lead to an increase in other symptoms through pem other symptoms of me cfs include you might experience frustration anxiety low mood anddepressionbecause of the impact of the condition on your life this does not mean that me cfs is a mental health condition read more about the symptoms of me cfs,,,
Chest infection,the main symptoms of a chest infection can include you may also experience more general symptoms of an infection such as aheadache fatigue sweating loss of appetite or joint and muscle pain many chest infections aren t serious and get better within a few days or weeks you won t usually need to see your gp unless your symptoms suggest you have a more serious infection while you recover at home there are things you can do to improve your symptoms avoid cough medicines as there s little evidence they work coughing actually helps you clear the infection more quickly by acquiring rid of the phlegm from your lungs antibioticsaren t recommended for many chest infections because they only work if the infection is caused by bacteria rather than a virus your gp will usually only prescribe antibiotic if they think you have pneumonia or you re at risk of complications such as fluid building up around the lungs pleurisy if there s a flu outbreak in your local area and you re at risk of serious infection your gp may also prescribe antiviral medication read more abouttreating bronchitisandtreating pneumonia,,,
