Chest infection,the main symptoms of a chest infection can include you may also experience more general symptoms of an infection such as aheadache fatigue sweating loss of appetite or joint and muscle pain many chest infections aren t serious and get better inside a few days or weeks you won t usually need to see your gp unless your symptoms suggest you have angstrom more serious infection while you recover at home there are things you can do to improve your symptoms avoid cough medicines as there s little evidence they work coughing actually helps you clear the infection more quickly by getting rid of the phlegm from your lungs antibioticsaren t recommended for many chest infections because they only work if the infection is caused by bacteria rather than a virus your gp will usually only prescribe antibiotics if they think you have pneumonia or you re at risk of complications such as fluid building up around the lungs pleurisy if there s a flu outbreak in your local area and you re at risk of serious infection your gp may also prescribe antiviral medication read more abouttreating bronchitisandtreating pneumonia,,,
