Gallstones,most cases of gallstones don t cause any symptoms but if a gallstone blocks one of the bile ducts it can cause sudden severe abdominal pain known as biliary colic other symptoms may develop if the blockage is more severe or develops in another part of the digestive system in a small number of people gallstone can cause more serious problems if they obstruct the flow of bile for longer periods or move into other organs such as the pancreas or small bowel if this happens you may develop doctor refer to this more severe condition as complicated gallstone disease read more about thecomplications of gallstones,,,
