Febrile seizures,the main symptom of a febrile seizure is a fit that occurs while a child has a fever febrile seizures often occur during the first day of a fever which is defined as a high temperature of 38c 100 4f or above however there appears to be no connection between the extent of your child s fever and the start of a seizure seizures can occur even if your child hour angle a mild fever simple febrile seizurescan happen when there s a rapid rise in temperature and you may only realise your child is ill when they have a fit alternatively they can occur as your child s temperature drops from a high level during simple febrile seizure complex febrile seizurestend to last longer than 15 minutes and the symptoms may only affect one area of your child s body the seizure sometimes recurs within 24 hours or during the period in which your child is ill,,,
Reactive arthritis,reactive arthritis most often affects the most people will not experience symptoms in all of these areas reactive arthritis can also cause symptoms including,"Reactive arthritis is usually linked to an infection. This includes: The body’s immune system seems to over-react to these infections. It then starts to attack healthy tissue, leading to inflammation. People with a gene known as HLA-B27 are also more likely to develop reactive arthritis. But, it’s not clear why this is the case.",,"There is no cure for reactive arthritis but the condition is usually temporary. Symptoms can often be controlled using: Severe symptoms may need to be manged with disease-modifying anti-rheumatic drugs (DMARDs). Antibioticsdon’t treat reactive arthritis itself. But, you may be prescribed antibiotics to treat an infection like an STI. Once your symptoms improve, it’s also helpful to begin some gentle exercise. Focus on strengthening the muscles and improving the range of motion in joints. Speak to a healthcare professional about exercises for you. You may be referred to a physiotherapist."
