Trigger thumb or trigger finger in children and young people,some common signs of trigger finger and thumb include,,,"Trigger thumb or finger in children usually gets better on its own with no treatment. This can take up to 2 years. There is no evidence that splinting, or exercise make any difference. Your child’s hand function won’t be affected while waiting for it to get better. In a very small number of cases where the trigger thumb or finger doesn’t resolve, surgery can be considered. Any surgery also comes with additional health risks. It’s not recommended for children under 3 years of age."
