Chronic fatigue syndrome,the symptoms of me cfs can be different for everyone there may be times when your symptoms improve and you ll be able to do some everyday activities at other times symptoms may get worse affecting your daily life not everyone will experience all of the symptoms if you experience new symptoms talk to your gp or specialist as the new symptoms may be unrelated to me cfs if you have periods you may find your symptoms get worse astatine different times during your menstrual cycle there are 4 main symptoms of me cfs me cfs can cause debilitating fatigue that is post exertional malaise pem is where symptoms get worse even after little physical or mental activity if you have pem you might find symptoms get worse hours or days after the activity you might find your symptoms are not in proportion to the amount of activity that has been done it can take a long time to recover from pem the symptoms might last hours days weeks or longer you might wake up feeling unrefreshed after sleep you might also experience sleep disturbance you might me cfs can cause cognitive trouble sometimes described as brain fog this can include simple physical or mental activities or combinations of activities can leave people with me cfs feeling completely exhausted it can also lead to an increase in other symptoms through pem other symptoms of me cfs include you might experience frustration anxiety low mood anddepressionbecause of the impact of the condition on your life this does not mean that me cfs is a mental health condition read more about the symptoms of me cfs,,,
Coronavirus (COVID-19),symptoms of coronavirus include less common symptoms include if you have symptoms of coronavirus you should you may still have acoughor feel tired after your other symptom have gone this doesn t mean that you re still infectious to others mostacute respiratory infectionslike coronavirus pass within 3 weeks there are some things you can do to help relieve your symptoms until the infection clears up antibiotics will not relieve your symptoms or speed up your recovery it s important to get help if you re at increased risk of becoming more unwell from coronavirus this includes if you re pregnant aged 60 or over or have a weaken immune system advice for people who may have coronavirus symptoms complete our self help guide to check your symptoms and find out what to do next there are things you can do to reduce the spread of coronavirus infection,,,
