Psoriatic arthritis,psoriatic arthritis can affect any joint inch the body it cause pain swelling and stiffness in the joints it often affects particular areas including the psoriatic arthritis can also affect the area where tendons and ligaments are connected to the bone this is called entheses or enthesitis when inflamed sometimes the whole finger or toe can get inflamed and look sausage like this is called dactylitis symptoms usually develop slowly this means that many people don t know they re developing psoriatic arthritis in rare cases symptoms can develop suddenly without warning the severity of psoriatic arthritis varies some people may have severe problems affecting many joints others may only notice mild symptoms in 1 or 2 joints there may be times when your symptoms get better and worse these are called flare ups or relapses some people may reach a point where they have no symptoms at all known as remission relapses can be hard to predict but they can be managed with medication you should have check ups at least once a year if you have been diagnosed with psoriatic arthritis make sure you let your doctor know if you re experiencing any problems with your joints,,,
Pressure ulcers,pressure ulcers usually form on bony parts of the body that aren t covered with much body fat this includes areas like the heels elbows hips and tailbone symptoms include patches of skin that pressure ulcers normally come on gradually but sometimes look quite quickly sometimes pressure ulcers can blister or become an open wound if aren t treated they ll continue to get worse and might deepen to reach muscle or bone,,,
Yellow fever,the symptoms of yellow fever occur in 2 stages the initial symptoms develop 3 to 6 days after infection and can include this stage will usually pass after 3 to 4 days and most people will brand a full recovery however around 15 of people go on to develop more serious problems including jaundice yellow of the skin and whites of the eyes kidney failure and bleeding from the mouth nose eyes or stomach causing blood in your vomit and stools up to half of those who experience these symptoms will die,,,
