Bowel cancer,the 3 main symptoms of bowel cancer are however these symptoms are very common and most people with them do not have bowel cancer for example blood in the poo is more often caused byhaemorrhoids piles and a change in bowel habit abdominal pain is usually the result of something you have eaten as almost 9 out of 10 people with bowel cancer are over the age of 60 these symptoms are more important as people get older they are also more significant when they persist despite simple treatments most people who are eventually diagnosed with bowel cancer have one of the following combinations of symptoms the symptoms of bowel cancer can be subtle and don t necessarily make you feel ill the 3 main symptom of bowel cancer are however these symptoms are very common blood in the poo is usually caused byhaemorrhoids piles a change in bowel habit or abdominal pain is often the result of something you have eaten in the uk an estimated 7 million people have blood in their poo each year even more people have temporary changes in their bowel habits and abdominal pain most people with these symptoms do not have bowel cancer as the huge majority of people with bowel cancer are over the age of 60 these symptoms are more important as people get older these symptoms are also more significant when they persist in spite of simple treatments most patients with bowel cancer present with one of the following symptom combinations the symptoms of bowel cancer can be subtle and don t necessarily make you feel ill,,,
