Skin cancer (melanoma),the first sign of a melanoma is often a new mole or a change in the appearance of an existing mole normal moles are usually round or oval with a smooth edge and no bigger than 6mm 1 4 inch in diameter speak to your gp as soon as possible if you notice changes in a mole freckle or patch of skin especially if the changes happen over a few weeks or months signs to look out for include a mole that is a helpful way to tell the difference between a normal mole and a melanoma is the abcde checklist melanomas can appear anywhere on your body but they most commonly appear on the back legs arms and face they may sometimes develop underneath a nail in rare cases melanoma can develop in the eye noticing angstrom dark spot or changes inch vision can be signs although it is more likely to be diagnosed during a routine eye examination read further information,,,
Motor neurone disease (MND),the symptoms of mnd start gradually over week and months they tend to appear on one side of the body first and get progressively worse there are usually 3 stages of symptoms sometimes the early symptoms are mistaken for similar conditions that also affect the nervous system as mnd becomes more advanced more parts and functions of the body are affected this can make you more likely to experience infections like chest infections which can cause your condition to get worse quicker as mnd progresses to its final phase you might experience eventually non invasive breathing assistance won t be enough to make up for the loss of normal lung function at this stage more medication can aid to reduce symptoms of breathlessness and anxiety related to it most people with mnd become increasingly drowsy before falling into a deep sleep where they usually die peacefully some people with mnd have other symptoms that aren t directly caused by the condition but are related to the stress of living with it these might includedepression insomniaandanxiety,,,
