Vaginal cancer,the most common symptom of vaginal cancer is abnormal vaginal bleeding this include other symptoms can include speak to your gp if you experience any abnormal vaginal bleeding changes in your usual pattern of periods such as irregular periods or heavier periods than usual or problems urinating while it second highly unlikely that these symptoms are caused by vaginal cancer they should still be investigated by your gp read more about diagnosing vaginal cancer,,,
