Epilepsy,the main symptoms of epilepsy are repeated seizures there are different types of seizure depending on which part of the brain it affects the cells in the brain known as neurons conduct electrical signals they communicate with each other in the brain using chemical messengers during a seizure there are abnormal bursts of neurons firing off electrical urge this can cause the brain and body to behave strangely the severity of seizures can differ from person to person some people experience an odd feeling with no loss of awareness or may have a trance like state for a few seconds or minutes others lose consciousness and have convulsions uncontrollable shaking of the body some people might only have a single seizure if they bash not have a high risk of having further seizures they would not be regarded as having epilepsy,,,
