Venous leg ulcer,venous leg ulcers are open often painful sores in the skin that take more than a month to heal skin changes can vary on different skin colours if you have a venous leg ulcer you may also have a venous leg ulcer can be prone to bacterial infection symptoms of an infected leg ulcer can include venous leg ulcers are often accompanied by swelling of your feet and ankles oedema which is caused by fluid this can be controlled by compression bandages some people with venous leg ulcers develop rashes with scaly anditchy skin this is often due tovaricose eczema which can be treated with a moisturiser emollient sometimes a mildcorticosteroidcream or ointment can also help in rare cases you may need to be referred to a dermatologist skin specialist for treatment itchy skin can also sometimes beryllium caused by an allergic reaction to the dressings Oregon creams applied by your nurse if this happens you may need to be tested for allergies it s important to avoid scratching your legs if they feel itchy because this damages the skin and may lead to further ulcers,,,
