Motor neurone disease (MND),the symptoms of mnd start gradually over weeks and months they tend to appear on one side of the body first and get progressively worse there are usually 3 stages of symptoms sometimes the early symptoms are mistaken for similar conditions that also affect the nervous system as mnd becomes more advanced more parts and functions of the body are affected this can make you more likely to experience infections like chest infections which can cause your condition to get worse quicker as mnd progresses to its final phase you might experience eventually non invasive breathing assistance won t be enough to make up for the loss of convention lung function at this stage more medication can help to reduce symptoms of breathlessness and anxiety related to it most people with mnd become increasingly drowsy before falling into a deep sleep where they usually die peacefully some people with mnd have other symptoms that aren t directly caused by the condition merely are related to the stress of living with it these might includedepression insomniaandanxiety,,,
