Vaginal cancer,the most common symptom of vaginal cancer is abnormal vaginal bleeding this includes other symptoms can include speak to your gp if you experience any abnormal vaginal bleeding changes in your usual form of periods such arsenic irregular periods or heavier periods than usual or problems urinating while it s highly unlikely that these symptoms are caused by vaginal cancer they should still be investigated by your gp read more about diagnosing vaginal cancer,,,
