Post-polio syndrome,the symptoms of post polio syndrome include the muscle weakness and atrophy usually affects muscles that were previously affected by polio sometimes it affects other muscles this can impact your mobility and your ability to do everyday tasks like brushing your teeth or drying your hair chronic fatigue is one of the most park and troublesome symptoms of post polio syndrome this can be physical fatigue tiredness and brain fatigue brain fatigue can cause problems with concentration attention and memory mri scanscan show white spots in the brains of polio survivors which may be related to brain fatigue the symptoms can gradually get worse over many years there are supportive treatments that can help with symptoms although post polio syndrome is rarely life threatening some people can develop breathing and swallowing difficulties that can lead to serious problems likechest infections some people experience a sensitivity to some type of anaesthesia causing them to take longer to recover from having anaesthesia,,,
