Supraventricular tachycardia,if you have supraventricular tachycardia you ll usually feel your heart racing in your chest Oregon throat the heart rate is usually between 140 to 180 beats per minute but can be as high as 250 a normal heartbeat should be 60 to 100 beats per minute at rest during a supraventricular tachycardia the heart muscle contracts very fast this means that it cannot relax properly between contractions to fill with blood this reduces the sum of blood being pumped around the body therefore you may also feel on rare occasions you may faint because of a drop in blood pressure these symptoms vary in length and frequency,,,
