Obstructive sleep apnoea,signs of osa can include some people with osa may also experience night sweats and may wake up frequently during the night to pee during an episode the lack of oxygen triggers your brain to pull you out of deep sleep either to a lighter sleep or to wakefulness your airway then reopens and you can breathe normally these repeated sleep interruptions can make you feel very tired and more likely to fall asleep during the day you ll usually have no memory of your interrupted breathing sol you may be unaware you have a problem,,,
