Coeliac disease,coeliac disease can cause a wide range of symptoms in the digestive system and rest of the body symptoms can develop at any age but coeliac disease is most commonly diagnosed between the ages of 40 and 60 years more about thesymptoms of coeliac diseaseorwhat is coeliac disease symptoms of coeliac disease vary from person to person and can range from mild to severe some people may have no symptom at all sometimes the symptoms of coeliac disease are mistaken for some common symptoms of coeliac disease include if you ve any of these symptoms speak to your gp you must continue eating gluten as part of your diet until you ve been diagnosed you can also take coeliac uk sonline assessment children with coeliac disease might also not grow at the expected rate or be late to range puberty,,,
Anorexia nervosa,anorexia nervosa can have a range of symptoms most of the time people won t have all of these symptom include you can never tell how unwell angstrom person is from just their weight or bmi in children with anorexia nervosa puberty and the associated growth spurt may be delayed they may gain less weight than expected for someone going through puberty,,,
