Peripheral neuropathy,symptoms of peripheral neuropathy can vary depending on which type you have they can also develop quickly or slowly the symptoms of mononeuropathy can vary because they depend on which specific nerve has been affected example symptoms could include even if the cause of your peripheral neuropathy cannot be treated you can get help with managing your symptoms if you re in pain you may be order different types of medication this is because standard painkillers like ibuprofen and paracetamol are often not effective at treating nerve pain if you re experiencing pain in a particular area of your body capsaicin cream may help capsaicin is the substance that makes chilli peppers hot it s thought to stop the nerves sending pain messages to the brain making it useful for nerve pain menthol cream can have a similar effect if your pain only affects a small area of skin you may be offered a Lidocaine plaster this is a large sticking plaster that contains a local anaesthetic which is absorbed into the skin the plaster covers if topical measures do not work your gp may consider a neuropathic agent these include some types of anti depressants if you re struggling with muscle weakness you may benefit from physiotherapy it can help improve weakness occupational therapycan help you find new ways of completing difficult tasks if you have foot drop or tripping orthotics can help with ankle supports if you re experiencing hyperhidrosis excessive sweating you may be offered botulinum toxin botox injections these could help reduce your sweating if you re struggling to empty your bladder you may be offered urodynamic studies depending on the result you may be offered medication orurinary catheterisationto help you,,,
Addison’s disease,addison s disease can be difficult to detect at first because early symptoms are similar to symptoms of many other health conditions initial symptoms of addison s disease can include dehydrationcan also be an early sign of addison s disease it s caused by lack of the hormone aldosterone in your body which is used to regulate the balance of salt and water further symptoms of addison s disease tend to develop gradually over months or years however additional stress caused by another illness or an accident for example may cause your symptoms to suddenly get worse you may go on to develop some woman may also have irregular periods or miss some periods completely children with addison s disease may experience puberty later than usual some people with addison s disease also developlow blood sugar hypoglycaemia this can cause symptoms such as difficulty concentrating confusion anxiety and even unconsciousness particularly in children if you re experiencing symptoms of addison s disease see your gp so they can diagnose or rule out the condition these symptoms will usually improve with appropriate treatment read more aboutdiagnosing addison second diseaseandtreating addison s disease,,,
