Malignant brain tumour (cancerous),the symptoms of a malignant brain tumour depend on how big it be and where it is in the brain common symptoms include speak to your gp if you have persistent symptoms of a brain tumour while it s unlikely to be a tumor it s best to be sure by getting a proper diagnosis read more about thesymptoms of malignant brain tumoursanddiagnosing malignant brain tumours the symptoms of a malignant brain tumour depend on how big it is and where it is in the brain when symptoms do occur it is because the brain tumour is either putting pressure on the brain or preventing an area of the brain from functioning properly different areas of the brain control different functions so the symptoms caused by a brain tumour will depend on where the tumour is located for example a tumour affecting you may also be given medication to relieve some of the symptoms you may have as a result of your brain tumour these may include depending on your circumstances these medications may be given before after or instead of surgery,,,
