Oculopharyngeal muscular dystrophy (OPMD),the symptoms of opmd are although you might have droopy eyelids your eyesight vision should not beryllium affected even when the condition worsens a person with opmd could have normal vision if their eyelids are raised worsening problems with swallowing dysphagia can cause problems swallowing fluids including saliva there s a danger of aspiration food drink or saliva going down the wrong way into the chest instead of the stomach this increases the risk of chest infections aspiration pneumonia some people with opmd experience muscle weakness first around the shoulders and then around the hips this doesn t usually happen until many years after the initial diagnosis it s usually mild but can progress to be more severe the life anticipation of someone with opmd is close to normal if it s managed well,,,
