Febrile seizures,the main symptom of a febrile seizure is a fit that occurs while a child has a fever febrile seizures often occur during the first day of a fever which is defined as angstrom high temperature of 38c 100 4f or above however there appears to be no connection between the extent of your child s fever and the start of a seizure seizures can occur even if your child has a mild fever simple febrile seizurescan happen when there s a rapid rise in temperature and you may only realise your child is ill when they have a fit alternatively they can occur as your child s temperature drops from a high level during simple febrile seizures complex febrile seizurestend to last longer than 15 minutes and the symptoms may only affect one area of your child s body the seizure sometimes recurs inside 24 hours or during the period in which your child is ill,,,
