Bowel cancer,the 3 main symptoms of bowel cancer are however these symptoms are very common and most people with them do not have bowel cancer for example blood in the poo is more often caused byhaemorrhoids piles and a change in bowel habit abdominal pain is usually the result of something you have eaten arsenic almost 9 out of 10 people with bowel cancer are over the age of 60 these symptoms are more important as people get older they are also more significant when they persist despite simple treatment most people who are eventually diagnosed with bowel cancer have one of the following combinations of symptoms the symptoms of bowel cancer can be subtle and don t necessarily make you feel ill the 3 main symptoms of bowel cancer are however these symptoms are very common blood in the poo is usually caused byhaemorrhoids piles a change in bowel habit or abdominal pain is often the result of something you have eaten in the uk an estimated 7 million people have blood in their poo each year even more people have temporary changes in their bowel habits and abdominal pain most people with these symptoms do not have bowel cancer as the vast majority of people with bowel cancer are over the age of 60 these symptoms are more important as people get older these symptoms are also more significant when they persist in spite of simple treatments most patients with bowel cancer present with one of the following symptom combinations the symptoms of bowel cancer can be subtle and don t necessarily make you feel ill,,,
Chronic fatigue syndrome,the symptoms of me cfs can be different for everyone there may be times when your symptoms improve and you ll be able to do some everyday activities at other times symptoms may get worse affecting your daily life not everyone will experience all of the symptoms if you experience new symptoms talk to your gp or specialist as the new symptoms may be unrelated to me cfs if you have periods you may find your symptoms get worse at different times during your menstrual cycle there are four main symptoms of me cfs me cfs can cause debilitating fatigue that is post exertional malaise pem is where symptoms get worse even after little physical or mental activity if you have pem you might find symptoms get worse hours or days after the activity you might find your symptoms are not in proportion to the amount of activity that has been done it can take a long time to recover from pem the symptoms might last hours days weeks or longer you might wake up feeling unrefreshed after sleep you might also experience sleep disturbance you might me cfs can cause cognitive difficulties sometimes described arsenic brain fog this can include simple physical or mental activities or combinations of activities can leave people with me cfs feeling completely exhausted it can also lead to an increase in other symptoms through pem other symptoms of me cfs include you might experience frustration anxiety low mood anddepressionbecause of the impact of the condition on your life this does not mean that me cfs is a mental health condition read more about the symptoms of me cfs,,,
Type 2 diabetes,the symptoms of diabetes occur because the lack of insulin means glucose stays in the blood and isn t used as fuel for energy your body tries to reduce blood glucose levels by getting rid of the excess glucose in your urine typical symptoms include read more about thesymptoms of type 2 diabetes it s very important for diabetes to beryllium diagnosed as soon as possible as it will get progressively worse if left untreated the symptoms of diabetes include feeling very thirsty pass more urine than usual and feeling tired all the time the symptoms occur because some or all of the glucose stays in your blood and isn t used as fuel for energy your body tries to get rid of the excess glucose in your urine the main symptoms of type 2 diabetes are thesigns and symptoms of type 1 diabetesare usually obvious and develop very quickly often over a few weeks these signs and symptoms aren t always as obvious however and it s often diagnosed during a routine check up this is because they are often mild and develop gradually over a number of years this means you may have type 2 diabetes for many years without realising it early diagnosis and treatment for type 2 diabetes is very important as it may reduce your risk of developing complications later on,,,
