Post-polio syndrome,the symptoms of post polio syndrome include the muscle weakness and atrophy usually affects muscles that were previously affected by polio sometimes it affects other muscles this can impact your mobility and your ability to do everyday tasks like brushing your teeth or drying your hair chronic fatigue is one of the most common and troublesome symptoms of post polio syndrome this can be physical fatigue tiredness and brain fatigue brain fatigue can cause problems with concentration attention and memory mri scanscan show white spots in the brains of polio survivors which may be associate to brain fatigue the symptoms can gradually get worse over many years there are supportive treatments that can help with symptoms although post polio syndrome is rarely life threatening some people can develop breathing and swallow difficulties that can lead to serious problems likechest infections some people experience a sensitivity to some types of anaesthesia causing them to take longer to recover from having anaesthesia,,,
Skin cancer (melanoma),the first sign of a melanoma is often a new mole or a change in the appearance of Associate in Nursing existing mole normal moles are usually round or oval with a smooth edge and no bigger than 6mm 1 4 inch in diameter speak to your gp as soon arsenic possible if you notice changes in a mole freckle or patch of skin especially if the changes happen over a few weeks or months signs to look out for include a mole that is a helpful way to tell the difference between a normal mole and a melanoma is the abcde checklist melanomas can appear anywhere on your body but they most commonly appear on the back legs arms and face they may sometimes develop underneath a nail in rare cases melanoma can develop in the eye noticing a dark spot or changes in vision can be signs although it is more likely to be diagnosed during a routine eye examination read further information,,,
