Restless legs syndrome,restless legs syndrome usually causes an overwhelming urge to move your legs it also causes an uncomfortable sensation in your legs which can affect your arms chest and face this sensation has been described as these unpleasant sensations can range from mild to severe they re usually worse in the evening and during the night the sensation can often be relieved by moving or rubbing your legs some people experience symptoms occasionally while others have them every day you may find it difficult to sit for long periods of time like on a long train journey up to 80 of people with restless legs syndrome also have periodic limb movements in sleep plms if you have plms your leg will jerk or twitch uncontrollably usually at night while you re asleep the movements are brief and repetitive and usually happen every 10 to 60 seconds plms can be severe enough to wake up both you and your partner the involuntary leg movements can also occur when you re awake and resting,,,"The treatment for restless legs syndrome can depend on: There are triggers that don’t cause restless legs syndrome, but can make symptoms worse. These include medications like: Other possible triggers of restless legs syndrome include: If your symptoms are mild, you may find that making a few lifestyle changes improves the syndrome. Having good sleep hygiene can help restless legs syndrome. This means that you have healthy sleep habits. During an episode of restless legs syndrome, the following measures may help relieve your symptoms: If primary restless legs syndrome is causing more severe symptoms, there are medications that may help. Your GP may suggest trying dopamine agonists, painkillers, hypnotics or levodopa. If your symptoms are caused by an underlying health problem, medical professionals will treat that health problem first. It may be that treating that problem will resolve the syndrome. Restless legs syndrome is not life threatening. Severe cases can disrupt sleep, causinginsomnia, and triggeranxietyanddepression."
